  "title": "The augmented triad",
  "summary": "Two major 3rds stacked: a dreamy, floating chord.",
  "minutes": 5,
  "steps": [
    {
      "type": "explain",
      "title": "Augmented triad",
      "body": "Stack two major 3rds and you get an **augmented triad**: root, major 3rd, and a raised 5th (8 half steps) above the root. C augmented is C E G♯. Its chord symbol is **Caug** or **C+**.\n\n**Why it matters:** It is rare, but it shows up as a dreamy, unsettled moment in ballads and old film music. If a chord sounds like it is floating, it may be augmented.",
